WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:04.170
New claims coming from Russia's
invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:08.008
The Russians are claiming just minutes ago
that there are Ukrainians

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:11.411
operating on the Russian side
of the border inside Russia.

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.980
We'll have much more on that
in just a moment.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.751
In the meantime, Ukrainian
officials are saying they still hold on

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:22.522
to some neighborhoods inside Bath Move,
which is that city in the Far East.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:24.858
The Russians claimed to have captured it.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.926
It has been
one of the most hotly contested

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:30.697
cities, the bloodiest
battlefields of the war in Ukraine.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:33.833
Ukrainian
President Zelensky mourned the devastation

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.869
there over the weekend.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:38.538
Mr. President,

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.774
this is less news,
but we're still in Ukraine's hands.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.611
The Russians say they take about one

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.981
I think no,

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:50.650
but you have to understand that
there is nothing.

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.218
They destroyed everything.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.787
There are no buildings.

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:55.722
It's a bit it's tragedy.

00:00:55.722 --> 00:01:00.927
But for today,
a moment is only in our cars.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:03.663
All right.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.366
CNN's Sam Kiley is in southeastern
Ukraine.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:09.202
Sam, back to what
we just reported a few moments ago.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:13.006
This claim from the Russians
that Belgorod, which is this city

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:15.308
over the border
from Ukraine that we showed on the map

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.310
a number of times,
just over the border from Ukraine.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:22.315
They say there are Ukrainian saboteurs
operating in and around that area.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.084
What can you tell us

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:27.921
Well,

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.990
the Ukrainians say, yeah, you're right,
except they're not Ukrainians.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.058
They're Russians.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:36.196
And they're saying indeed that
and the unit themselves

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:40.767
have put out a video saying that they are
involved in this cross-border operation

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.770
because they're members of the Freedom
from Russia Legion,

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:48.975
which is a group of Russian volunteers
who are in the Ukrainian armed forces.

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.810
They have in the past been fighting.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.247
When I encountered them back in December,
they were fighting very heavily

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:57.383
as south of parliament on the front line
there.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.487
It now
appears that they have crossed into Russia

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.423
with an all Russian team,
according to the Ukrainians,

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.726
and the Ukrainian government
is saying somewhat coyly

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:09.796
that they are operating there
entirely as Russian

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:13.967
citizens, as free agents,
not as part of the Ukrainian armed forces.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:14.868
Although, of course,

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:19.405
they're using Ukrainian uniforms,
weapons, bullets and arguably vehicles.

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:23.643
Now, that spokesman
or that the member of their political wing

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:27.780
here in Ukraine has told CNN
that the combat is ongoing.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.751
And certainly social media would indicate
from a number of videos

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:34.621
that are being posted
that they have deployed themselves

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.190
in a number of villages
very close to the border.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:42.128
This is the first time that we have
confirmation from the Ukrainians that,

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:47.300
let's say a Ukrainian backed organization,
military organization, has conducted

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:52.872
overt military action against Russia
inside Russian territory.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:56.009
We've seen in the past covert
military operations

00:02:56.009 --> 00:03:00.980
deep behind Russian lines here in Ukraine
and indeed mysterious activities

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:04.651
inside Russia itself that have even been
helicopter gunship attacks

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.553
close to the city of Belgorod

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:10.623
in the past that the Ukrainians
have refused to acknowledge.

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.458
But this is a first. John.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.027
Yes, and let me just point out
on the map here

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:15.662
so people can see
if we keep talking about it,

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:19.332
this is build a road right here,
right over the border from Ukraine there.

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:23.136
And a first, as you note,
a first of the Ukrainians confirming that

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:26.606
at least at a minimum,
pro-Ukrainian forces are operating

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.107
inside Russian territory.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:30.843
Sam, calling it significant development.
We'll come back to you in a bit.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.612
Thank you. Let's bring in retired U.S.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:35.448
Army Major Mike Lyons. It's
good to have you as always.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:39.385
So let's begin
there because Zelensky saying

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.156
not for
sure, the buck has fallen to the Russians.

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:45.825
Russia,
the volunteer group is saying it has.

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:46.826
Why is it significant?

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:49.862
Not strategically,
but began to watch propaganda.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:50.830
That's all it's going on here.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.565
This is the twilight part of this battle.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:53.399
At this point, there's

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:56.769
no nothing tactically more to be gained
that the city has been flattened.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.638
Fundamentally, it's more or less.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:02.408
It shows Ukrainian resilience,
but also Russian military failure.

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:05.445
They're trying to claim some kind of
victory right now that just isn't there.

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:08.581
So also a shift in the Biden
administration's

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:11.618
views on F-16s over the weekend.

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:12.285
Right.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:16.756
At least greenlighting joint
training of F-16 pilots

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:19.592
with our European allies.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.960
Why is that significant?

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.061
Because as you know, The Wall Street

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.897
Journal editorial board very critical
that it's taken this long.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.466
They write about it.

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:30.136
The obvious question is why
this decision took 15 months.

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:31.371
Yeah, well, a couple of things.

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:32.905
First of all, let's be clear
right about this.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:36.276
The F-16s are not going to be game
changing to the situation on the ground.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:39.012
It's not going to give air superiority
to the Ukraine military.

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:41.014
There's going to be a very long time
before

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:42.815
they're actually going to be impactful.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:46.052
I think it took that long
because from a strategic perspective, now

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:48.187
you're going to see Ukraine eventually.

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:50.590
And NATO's
this is really kind of a fait accompli.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.959
Now because of them getting this platform.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:56.262
So because of fighter jets,
not previous weapons like Mars, etc..

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.031
Now, this is a strategic weapon.

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:02.802
So like, for example, he Zelensky tells
President Biden he's not going to attack

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:06.372
into Russia because the F-16 gives him
that capability,

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:10.109
hard border right around between
Ukraine and Russia here.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.878
There's targets in Belgorod.

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:16.949
There's air base targets here, missile
sites along along this border here.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:21.654
There's multiple sites
that the F-16 now has capability to attack

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:25.358
that cross that border and that
that violates that's where that from.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:28.528
These weapons were supposed
to be defensive, now become offensive.

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:32.598
Looking at the countries where it's likely
that the F-16s would come

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:34.734
from the United States, what?

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:39.038
So I think these four countries are
the ones that likely give up the F-16s

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:43.076
they have in their inventory
as they transition to F-35s.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:46.279
Norway, Denmark,
the Netherlands and Belgium,

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:47.747
maybe

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:50.883
30 to
60 or so F-16s in the next few months.

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:53.419
It's still going to take
a significant amount of time.

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:55.321
Three major issues
here. We've got to train pilots.

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.957
We have to make sure the pilots
are up to speed on what's going on.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.125
That's going to be four to six months.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.427
And it's it's a surmountable challenge
right now.

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:04.030
But maintenance and sustainability of
these is going to be a key.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.265
There's some spare parts
that they're not even made anymore.

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.468
Lastly,
what are the munitions going to look like?

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:09.902
What are those
airframes are going to be on them

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:12.472
because the F-16 is a platform,
does a lot of different thing.

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:16.209
Note it, this pilot training is a reason
why a number of members of Congress,

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:18.444
actually Republicans were calling
on the Biden administration

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:21.981
to start the training Earlier,
in case we got to this point.

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:23.683
Let's talk
about what was signed overnight.

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:26.152
The president
had to cancel his leg of this trip

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:29.288
so he didn't go for a first ever
what would have been a historic visit

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:31.324
first American president
to go to Papua New Guinea.

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:32.592
But Secretary Blinken went.

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:33.493
Yep. And overnight

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:38.131
